DESCRIPTION:When: Saturday\, November 21st\, 2026\, 11am–2pm.\nWhere: Bl
 ack Point Historic Gardens - Van Ness Side\n\nJoin the Parks Conservancy t
 o celebrate 5 years of the Black Point Historic Gardens being open to the 
 public after 50 years of abandonment behind fences. Come out to the garden
  to explore the plants\, animals\, and activities that make this space spe
 cial. Take part in a guided bird walk\, slow down with a meditation\, or g
 et to know this special area with creative nature-based activities for the
  whole family!\n\nInterested in gardening with native plants? Fall is the 
 best time to start planning and planting native plants in your garden. We 
 have can help you learn how and will be giving away FREE native wildflower
  seeds while supplies last.\n\nStop by to explore or bring a picnic and st
 ay a while! Feel free to drop by anytime between 11am–2pm and register t
 o receive updates about the event.\n\nFree\nGolden Gate National Parks Con
 servancy\n\nTickets: https://www.parksconservancy.org/events/fort-mason/fa
 lling-native-plants?utm_source=dothebay&utm_medium=web&utm_campaign=fallin
 g_plants&utm_content=listing_112126\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/
 2026/11/21/falling-for-native-plants-at-fort-mason-tickets\nSource: DoTheB
 ay\n\nAlso listed on:\n- https://sf.funcheap.com/2026-fall-native-plant-fe
 st-free-wildflower-seeds-fort-mason-gardens-sf/
